=== provenance ===
Host:    intel-lo@surface, c7i.2xlarge (8 vCPU), x86_64,
         Amazon Linux 2023, gcc 11.5.0, glibc 2.34, gdb 14.2, libnuma present
Runner:  scripts/ec2/job.sh intel-lo@surface start ph4final 5400 \
             './scripts/ec2/verify_phase4.sh'
Script:  scripts/ec2/verify_release_artifacts.sh covers the same dist/install
         ground standalone; scripts/ec2/verify_phase4.sh is the full matrix.

=== what this run establishes ===
  * default build: make check 8/8, and the new hash-partition regression
    passes (its pre-fix control fails 7 checks -- see
    prefix-evidence/2026-09-21-hash-partition-prefix-control.log).
  * a default build is AVX2-free: no -mavx2 on any command line and
    HAVE_AVX2 undefined, so it cannot SIGILL on pre-Haswell x86-64.
  * --enable-avx2 does pass -mavx2 and still passes 8/8.
  * --enable-percpu-caching and --enable-htm are gone from configure --help,
    the former is reported as unrecognized, and UMEM_PER_CPU_CACHE cannot be
    defined by any flag.
  * every remaining feature flag builds and passes: --enable-rseq,
    --disable-rseq (builds now; see the KNOWN note), --enable-numa,
    --disable-numa, --enable-avx2, --enable-introspect.
  * make dist produces a tarball that configures, builds, passes make check
    8/8, builds test/property/prop_palloc (the examples/umem_palloc.c
    EXTRA_DIST fix), and passes install-check.
  * install-check: an external program compiles and links against nothing but
    the installed prefix, the installed umem(1) runs, and umemctl is
    installed.

=== the one KNOWN-PREEXISTING entry ===
--disable-rseq reports make check 7/8.  The sole failure is
test/debugger/test_inspect_e2e.sh's cached_skipped == 2 assertion, which is
pre-existing and deterministic in that configuration (12/12), and fails
2/12 even in a default build.  Proven independent of this workstream by
rebuilding the pre-Phase-4 tree: 8/8 failures.  See
2026-09-21-make-check-flaky-inspect-e2e.log.  Counted separately from PASS
and from FAIL, and deliberately NOT retried.

=== not covered by this run ===
  * aarch64.  Nothing here was verified on arm-lo/arm-hi.
  * the non-Linux platforms (FreeBSD, illumos, macOS, Windows).
  * --enable-asan / --enable-ubsan / --enable-tsan / --enable-pgo builds.
  * anything beyond make check's 8 entries: test_main, the property tests,
    the concurrency oracle, and the stress suites were not run here.
